  "id": "hyperliquid",
  "category": "exchange",
  "summary": "Hyperliquid's API on mainnet: perpetuals. An order is typed with its value in USDC, price times size, on the perpetual its asset number names (table perps, from the exchange's meta, whose numbers only ever grow). Several orders in one request, spot assets, builder fees, market trigger orders and TWAPs are refused, as are leverage and margin changes, moving funds out, and account control (agents, builder fees, sub-accounts, multi-sig). Cancels are typed; reads (/info) pass.",
